WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.640
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:02.910 --> 00:03.600
Hey!

3
00:03.970 --> 00:05.920
You were right to come to my mother for advice.

4
00:05.940 --> 00:08.240
With ten years of experience being nosy,

5
00:09.010 --> 00:10.010
my mom

6
00:10.040 --> 00:12.220
is practically an all-knowing deity.

7
00:12.990 --> 00:15.410
Even an all-knowing deity can't compare to "All-Knowing Duang."

8
00:16.270 --> 00:17.000
All-knowing Duang.

9
00:17.080 --> 00:17.720
- Yes? - Oh?

10
00:17.850 --> 00:19.010
You know everything?

11
00:19.040 --> 00:19.690
Everything.

12
00:20.430 --> 00:21.700
- You know about women? - Of course.

13
00:21.850 --> 00:23.060
- You know about men? - Of course.

14
00:23.220 --> 00:25.040
Then do you know where your husband is?

15
00:25.090 --> 00:26.370
Go ask your father.

16
00:26.510 --> 00:27.410
- Whoa... - Hey.

17
00:27.430 --> 00:29.050
All-knowing Dolly was just kidding.

18
00:29.070 --> 00:31.010
Don't crash out yet.

19
00:31.030 --> 00:32.570
Let's not joke around.

20
00:32.619 --> 00:33.630
Please help us out first.

21
00:33.820 --> 00:36.140
We've stared at this footage until our eyes hurt,

22
00:36.250 --> 00:39.330
but we still can't tell who the person is.

23
00:39.350 --> 00:40.480
Leave it to me.

24
00:40.500 --> 00:41.050
Alright.

25
00:41.280 --> 00:42.560
If they live in this dorm,

26
00:42.580 --> 00:45.300
I can identify them and their room by their leg hair.

27
00:45.550 --> 00:46.930
Whoa...

28
00:46.960 --> 00:48.560
- We're on the right track. - Ooh, there's hope.

29
00:49.030 --> 00:49.670
Alright, alright.

30
00:49.710 --> 00:50.230
Let's see.

31
01:08.830 --> 01:10.480
Oh, she's good at this.

32
01:11.590 --> 01:12.380
You know who they are, right?

33
01:12.400 --> 01:13.039
Not at all.

34
01:13.060 --> 01:14.060
- Huh? - What?

35
01:14.350 --> 01:16.300
They covered themselves completely.

36
01:16.470 --> 01:19.450
I can't even spot a single leg hair, so how would I know who they are?

37
01:19.630 --> 01:20.480
Mm...

38
01:20.880 --> 01:22.420
Aren't there any other camera angles?

39
01:22.590 --> 01:24.250
The hard drive was damaged.

40
01:24.510 --> 01:26.990
The handyman said we're lucky to have recovered this footage at all.

41
01:27.010 --> 01:27.850
Oh...

42
01:28.039 --> 01:29.320
They look familiar, though.

43
01:29.440 --> 01:30.230
- Hm? - Yeah?

44
01:30.250 --> 01:31.700
I think I saw

45
01:32.200 --> 01:35.050
someone dressed like this when Dollar forced me to work out.

46
01:35.560 --> 01:36.250
Oh?

47
01:40.289 --> 01:41.220
Oh!

48
01:41.240 --> 01:42.060
I remember now.

49
01:44.900 --> 01:46.380
He lives in Room 407.

50
01:46.620 --> 01:47.750
- What?! - Huh?!

51
01:48.020 --> 01:48.900
Are you sure?

52
01:48.920 --> 01:49.640
I am.

53
01:49.800 --> 01:51.830
I still vividly remember

54
01:51.850 --> 01:53.240
seeing that thing dangling

55
01:53.380 --> 01:55.320
as I ran past him.

56
01:55.450 --> 01:56.490
- What?! - Huh?!

57
01:56.509 --> 01:57.320
What was dangling?

58
01:57.340 --> 01:59.420
A keychain with a room number tag.

59
01:59.440 --> 02:00.640
- Oh... - Oh...

60
02:00.660 --> 02:01.370
A room number tag.

61
02:01.390 --> 02:02.880
You said something was dangling, so I thought you meant eggs.

62
02:03.000 --> 02:03.930
- What?! - Huh?!

63
02:03.990 --> 02:04.780
What eggs?

64
02:04.800 --> 02:05.690
Boiled eggs.

65
02:05.710 --> 02:07.240
Runners tend to bring them along when they run.

66
02:07.260 --> 02:08.050
- Oh... - Oh...

67
02:08.070 --> 02:09.449
- Eating it as they run? - Eating it as they run.

68
02:09.470 --> 02:10.090
Probably two eggs.

69
02:10.110 --> 02:12.490
Dobby, you do not need to ask them anything else.

70
02:12.750 --> 02:14.650
Knowing the room number is enough.

71
02:16.210 --> 02:17.030
Ms. Danis,

72
02:17.050 --> 02:19.000
do you know the tenant in Room 407?

73
02:20.350 --> 02:21.700
I've heard of him, though.

74
02:21.950 --> 02:23.640
He's a loner.

75
02:23.660 --> 02:25.450
And whenever he goes anywhere,

76
02:25.930 --> 02:27.190
he drags a suitcase along.

77
02:27.430 --> 02:29.390
- A huge one, too. - Mm.

78
02:29.410 --> 02:30.600
I don't know where he's going.

79
02:30.930 --> 02:31.940
Sadhu!

80
02:32.160 --> 02:36.250
I hope we finally find Grandma Gaysorn.

81
02:36.500 --> 02:37.510
If we do meet her,

82
02:37.680 --> 02:41.410
I'll have my mom do a pole dance for Gramps.

83
02:41.760 --> 02:42.780
What do you mean, pole dance?

84
02:42.910 --> 02:43.960
I'm your mother,

85
02:43.980 --> 02:45.320
not a suckling pig from Uncle Rong's Kitchen.

86
02:45.710 --> 02:46.770
Are you crazy?

87
02:46.790 --> 02:47.250
Let's go.

88
02:47.270 --> 02:48.230
Let's go to Room 407.

89
02:48.250 --> 02:49.300
- Let's go to Ratchaburi. - What?

90
02:49.320 --> 02:50.300
To the pig at Uncle Rong's Kitchen.

91
02:50.480 --> 02:51.200
Why are we going there?

92
02:51.310 --> 02:51.829
Why not?

93
02:51.850 --> 02:53.430
Well, everyone who ate there got diarrhea.

94
02:53.710 --> 02:54.930
- What? - What?

95
02:54.950 --> 02:56.520
Uh, but they've fixed the recipe.

96
02:56.540 --> 02:58.190
Not as many people get diarrhea now.

97
03:02.650 --> 03:06.180
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

98
03:06.200 --> 03:10.460
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

99
03:12.480 --> 03:18.750
♫Every step we take has a meaning♫

100
03:19.620 --> 03:24.790
♫No path is ever meaningless♫

101
03:26.810 --> 03:33.130
♫As long as our hearts keep searching♫

102
03:33.900 --> 03:38.380
♫One day, we'll find what we're yearning for♫

103
03:38.400 --> 03:42.030
♫Walking alone is fine, but it's better when you're by my side♫

104
03:42.050 --> 03:45.620
♫It won't be lonely when you're here to walk beside♫

105
03:45.640 --> 03:48.380
♫Like a love that waits, waits at the D Dorm♫

106
03:49.210 --> 03:51.300
♫Like a love that remains, remains at the dorm♫

107
03:51.320 --> 03:58.570
♫Meaningful love and good things await on every path♫

108
03:58.590 --> 04:05.770
♫It might not be a coincidence that we get to meet♫

109
04:05.790 --> 04:12.970
♫There might be hidden meanings on the path beneath our feet♫

110
04:12.990 --> 04:20.190
♫Perhaps the D Dorm is what led me to meet you♫

111
04:20.220 --> 04:23.880
[The D Dorm]

112
04:32.650 --> 04:33.850
Maybe no one's home.

113
04:34.260 --> 04:35.050
Should we...

114
04:35.340 --> 04:36.460
leave him a note?

115
04:36.480 --> 04:37.450
That way, he can get back to us.

116
04:37.700 --> 04:38.960
Didn't Ms. Danis say

117
04:39.150 --> 04:42.250
the tenant in this room carries a huge suitcase everywhere?

118
04:42.540 --> 04:43.430
What if he's gone for a month?

119
04:43.450 --> 04:44.280
Oh, right...

120
04:44.520 --> 04:45.500
Don't worry.

121
04:46.390 --> 04:47.220
Here.

122
04:49.100 --> 04:50.170
I have the spare keys.

123
04:50.190 --> 04:51.420
- Let's just unlock it, then. - Yeah.

124
04:55.620 --> 04:56.650
Yes, Director?

125
04:57.040 --> 04:58.150
There's a retake today?

126
04:59.320 --> 05:00.480
I won't be able to make it.

127
05:01.300 --> 05:03.250
I have something important to help my best friend with.

128
05:03.270 --> 05:04.480
Mm, well said.

129
05:05.050 --> 05:05.980
Thanks, my dude.

130
05:06.000 --> 05:07.270
You're paying me 3,000?!

131
05:07.450 --> 05:09.160
Oh... He isn't my best friend.

132
05:09.250 --> 05:10.220
We're not that close.

133
05:12.820 --> 05:13.640
Dobby, I have to go.

134
05:14.020 --> 05:15.160
What? Dax?!

135
05:15.470 --> 05:16.300
Dax!

136
05:16.320 --> 05:18.850
Some friend you have, huh?

137
05:18.870 --> 05:20.460
Money really talks, doesn't it?

138
05:21.680 --> 05:22.500
How about this?

139
05:23.160 --> 05:26.160
I will check inside the room first.

140
05:26.180 --> 05:27.110
Go on, Grandpa.

141
05:30.250 --> 05:31.790
Why is this room so empty?

142
05:32.220 --> 05:35.240
There's barely anything here. Does anyone even live here?

143
05:35.480 --> 05:37.200
There is not even a single photo.

144
05:38.360 --> 05:42.040
How would I know if he is related to Gaysorn?

145
05:43.150 --> 05:45.110
Why is this so stiff?

146
05:56.880 --> 05:58.760
A killer...

147
06:00.170 --> 06:01.670
Got it open.

148
06:02.210 --> 06:04.750
We are screwed!

149
06:08.570 --> 06:09.710
Dobby, run!

150
06:09.750 --> 06:10.410
Run!

151
06:10.430 --> 06:11.140
Run from what, Grandpa?

152
06:11.160 --> 06:12.830
There is a killer in there.

153
06:13.620 --> 06:14.550
Run!

154
06:14.570 --> 06:15.970
- A killer? - A killer!

155
06:15.990 --> 06:16.460
Run!

156
06:16.480 --> 06:16.990
Whoa.

157
06:17.440 --> 06:19.150
Come on, Grandpa!

158
06:28.740 --> 06:29.750
- Grandpa. - Mm.

159
06:30.040 --> 06:31.760
Someone was standing in the bathroom with a knife?

160
06:31.780 --> 06:32.550
Mm.

161
06:32.760 --> 06:33.900
Are you sure you weren't seeing things?

162
06:33.920 --> 06:35.120
I am sure of it.

163
06:35.140 --> 06:36.830
I saw him with my own eyes.

164
06:36.880 --> 06:38.710
He was hiding in the bathroom.

165
06:38.750 --> 06:41.070
When you tried to open the door,

166
06:41.120 --> 06:42.760
he grabbed the knife...

167
06:42.780 --> 06:44.470
and got ready to stab you.

168
06:44.820 --> 06:45.590
Why...

169
06:45.770 --> 06:47.110
did he want to stab me, though?

170
06:47.159 --> 06:48.310
How would I know?!

171
06:49.310 --> 06:51.200
He might've gotten annoyed

172
06:51.220 --> 06:53.220
because you kept knocking

173
06:53.240 --> 06:54.310
on his door.

174
06:55.040 --> 06:56.760
You had better stay away from that room.

175
06:56.780 --> 06:59.510
Then how are we supposed to find out about Grandma Gaysorn?

176
06:59.810 --> 07:00.910
Because he...

177
07:01.110 --> 07:03.430
was the one who dropped her photo.

178
07:04.830 --> 07:06.160
I think the tenant in that room

179
07:06.880 --> 07:08.420
is dangerous.

180
07:10.830 --> 07:12.510
I do not want you to risk it.

181
07:19.600 --> 07:20.400
Are you...

182
07:20.920 --> 07:22.160
worried about me?

183
07:25.950 --> 07:27.310
Maybe I am worried about a dog?

184
07:28.250 --> 07:31.350
What if it scratched its leprous skin, causing it to bleed to death?

185
07:32.710 --> 07:35.100
You should wait until Dax gets back.

186
07:35.120 --> 07:36.990
If you got stabbed,

187
07:37.060 --> 07:39.600
your mother would curse me.

188
07:39.620 --> 07:40.520
- Fine. - Alright?

189
07:40.540 --> 07:42.010
I'll wait until Dax comes back.

190
07:42.030 --> 07:42.740
Very good.

191
07:42.760 --> 07:44.150
- Then we'll go together. - Yeah.

192
07:47.510 --> 07:49.070
[The D Dorm]

193
07:49.200 --> 07:49.900
Grandpa,

194
07:50.420 --> 07:52.530
is this the person who was holding a knife

195
07:52.560 --> 07:53.430
in Room 407?

196
07:57.040 --> 07:57.750
Whoa...

197
07:59.630 --> 08:00.750
I am not sure.

198
08:00.990 --> 08:02.860
You were a bad person when you were alive.

199
08:03.300 --> 08:04.420
And now that you're a ghost,

200
08:04.440 --> 08:06.270
you have bad eyesight, too, huh?

201
08:06.790 --> 08:08.170
How would I know?

202
08:08.190 --> 08:11.080
He wore a hood and a face mask.

203
08:11.100 --> 08:12.970
How would I recognize his face?

204
08:12.990 --> 08:13.750
So feisty.

205
08:13.950 --> 08:17.230
I should have let you get stabbed to death.

206
08:18.380 --> 08:20.390
If I die, I'll still stay by your side.

207
08:21.520 --> 08:22.790
- Dobby. - Huh?

208
08:23.140 --> 08:25.060
Have you talked to the tenant in Room 407 yet?

209
08:25.550 --> 08:27.270
So, is he Grandma Gaysorn's grandson?

210
08:27.880 --> 08:28.970
I haven't talked to him yet.

211
08:29.540 --> 08:30.380
I already went up there,

212
08:30.660 --> 08:31.350
but he wasn't home.

213
08:31.480 --> 08:32.789
Why don't we go up there today, then?

214
08:33.070 --> 08:34.000
He might be home.

215
08:34.309 --> 08:34.850
Come on.

216
08:34.870 --> 08:35.710
Don't!

217
08:37.390 --> 08:38.210
It's too risky.

218
08:51.960 --> 08:52.680
Oh...

219
08:54.170 --> 08:56.670
What was that about it being risky again?

220
08:56.720 --> 08:58.000
Oh, I mean...

221
08:58.320 --> 08:59.470
I don't want you to risk falling down the stairs.

222
08:59.870 --> 09:02.410
Do you know how many people fall down the stairs each year?

223
09:02.430 --> 09:03.060
- Do you? - I don't know.

224
09:03.080 --> 09:03.560
What?

225
09:03.900 --> 09:04.720
And do you?

226
09:04.740 --> 09:05.680
- You're asking me? - Mm.

227
09:06.670 --> 09:07.200
I don't know either.

228
09:07.780 --> 09:08.690
Then why did you say that?

229
09:08.710 --> 09:10.470
I just don't want you to fall down the stairs.

230
09:10.580 --> 09:12.170
You should work here.

231
09:12.560 --> 09:14.210
Leave Room 407 to me.

232
09:14.230 --> 09:15.220
Danis, Danis.

233
09:15.240 --> 09:15.750
Huh?

234
09:15.770 --> 09:17.200
Danis, have you seen the news?

235
09:17.780 --> 09:19.730
Our dorm has a dismemberment case. [Locals Terrified! Dismemberment Killer Still at Large]

236
09:19.750 --> 09:20.790
Most importantly,

237
09:20.840 --> 09:23.470
Dollar said the culprit is still hiding near our dorm.

238
09:23.510 --> 09:25.230
Huh? Really?

239
09:25.640 --> 09:28.970
Is that the killer in Room 407?

240
09:29.750 --> 09:31.150
Could they be hiding in our dorm?

241
09:31.260 --> 09:33.190
Exactly...

242
09:36.980 --> 09:37.650
Whoa...

243
09:37.670 --> 09:38.740
A dismemberment killer.

244
09:38.760 --> 09:39.870
That's brutal.

245
09:43.230 --> 09:43.760
Oops!

246
09:43.780 --> 09:45.310
Oh... Oh, I'm sorry.

247
09:45.770 --> 09:46.510
I'm sorry.

248
09:52.160 --> 09:52.720
Whoa!

249
09:54.540 --> 09:55.150
You are...

250
09:59.110 --> 09:59.710
Huh?

251
10:00.990 --> 10:01.960
I thought I heard Dax.

252
10:03.200 --> 10:04.270
Was I hearing things?

253
10:04.870 --> 10:05.900
Ow, ow.

254
10:07.390 --> 10:08.610
I'm sorry. I really am.

255
10:08.630 --> 10:11.080
Don't worry, I won't tell anyone

256
10:11.100 --> 10:11.990
that you are...

257
10:15.750 --> 10:21.110
♫You cutie pie, you make me fall so madly in love♫

258
10:21.140 --> 10:22.750
Ugh, stop it already.

259
10:31.640 --> 10:34.600
[Disney, occupation: beloved superstar]

260
10:34.700 --> 10:35.380
Have a seat.

261
10:36.160 --> 10:36.990
Uh...

262
10:37.360 --> 10:38.950
Have a seat. Don't be shy.

263
10:39.190 --> 10:40.230
I'm not shy.

264
10:40.960 --> 10:41.710
But...

265
10:41.940 --> 10:42.950
your bed...

266
10:43.130 --> 10:45.310
reminds me of a series you've been in before.

267
10:46.420 --> 10:47.110
"Hia...

268
10:47.810 --> 10:48.910
Aren't we really going to...

269
10:51.530 --> 10:52.630
tonight?"

270
10:54.390 --> 10:55.310
See?

271
10:55.360 --> 10:57.230
I'm a big fan of yours.

272
10:57.250 --> 10:59.350
I've seen everything. I know every line.

273
10:59.570 --> 11:00.360
Thank you.

274
11:00.380 --> 11:01.830
My name is Dax.

275
11:01.850 --> 11:03.090
I'm a supporting actor.

276
11:03.320 --> 11:04.470
Mr. Disney...

277
11:04.490 --> 11:06.360
you're my superstar, my idol.

278
11:06.380 --> 11:09.400
I've always dreamed of being in a series with you.

279
11:09.420 --> 11:10.650
It can be any series.

280
11:11.230 --> 11:13.650
I could even play a zombie in 'Zomvivor.'

281
11:21.380 --> 11:22.390
Is he all there...?

282
11:22.840 --> 11:23.670
Pardon?

283
11:24.230 --> 11:25.020
Oh...

284
11:25.340 --> 11:26.210
I said...

285
11:26.230 --> 11:29.110
if you get the chance, please do your best.

286
11:29.350 --> 11:30.420
Of course I will.

287
11:32.000 --> 11:32.730
By the way...

288
11:33.030 --> 11:34.670
why are you here?

289
11:34.820 --> 11:36.310
You're in Room 407, too.

290
11:36.550 --> 11:37.890
Are you Grandma Gaysorn's relative?

291
11:38.690 --> 11:40.000
Grandma Gaysorn?

292
11:41.190 --> 11:43.590
This room is actually my manager's.

293
11:44.060 --> 11:46.150
But they're at the temple observing the precepts right now.

294
11:46.610 --> 11:48.200
When will they be back?

295
11:48.750 --> 11:50.430
I have to ask them something.

296
11:50.860 --> 11:52.310
I'm not sure either.

297
11:53.400 --> 11:57.670
But you have to keep it a secret that I'm living here.

298
11:57.760 --> 11:58.970
Not a word to anyone.

299
11:58.990 --> 12:00.590
I want to keep to myself and rehearse my script.

300
12:00.800 --> 12:02.090
I just want some time alone.

301
12:03.070 --> 12:03.990
Don't tell anyone.

302
12:07.710 --> 12:09.380
Who says you have to be alone,Your Highness?

303
12:10.180 --> 12:11.890
I will stay by your side.

304
12:14.110 --> 12:15.090
See?

305
12:15.110 --> 12:16.940
I remember every line from every series you've been in.

306
12:19.210 --> 12:20.230
To be honest,

307
12:20.290 --> 12:23.550
I'm not a fan of the actor who played the royal guard.

308
12:23.930 --> 12:26.350
I think he tried a bit too hard to look cool.

309
12:27.230 --> 12:28.630
If he's as handsome as I am, that's another story.

310
12:28.960 --> 12:29.710
Huh?

311
12:31.710 --> 12:32.730
So...

312
12:33.110 --> 12:35.010
you promise to keep this a secret, right?

313
12:35.190 --> 12:35.980
I promise!

314
12:37.840 --> 12:40.720
[DO-MUN-DRIP]

315
12:44.970 --> 12:45.960
Wow...

316
12:45.980 --> 12:49.070
The mangoes from the farm your mother owns are amazing.

317
12:49.130 --> 12:50.960
What type of mango is this? It's so nutty.

318
12:50.980 --> 12:51.830
Over 1,000 Thai baht.

319
12:52.490 --> 12:53.110
Ugh...

320
12:53.470 --> 12:54.400
He's asking about the type.

321
12:54.420 --> 12:55.640
- The type? - Yeah.

322
12:55.670 --> 12:57.590
- I thought he asked about the price. - No.

323
12:57.610 --> 12:58.470
Tell him, tell him.

324
12:58.490 --> 13:00.270
It'd be too easy to just tell you.

325
13:00.290 --> 13:01.340
Let's play a game.

326
13:01.360 --> 13:02.550
I'll give you a hint.

327
13:02.570 --> 13:04.890
If you can guess correctly, I'll give you two mangoes.

328
13:05.130 --> 13:06.140
- Okay. - Are you in?

329
13:06.160 --> 13:06.990
Yes, yes, yes.

330
13:07.010 --> 13:08.910
Here's a hint about

331
13:08.930 --> 13:10.110
the mango you're eating...

332
13:10.340 --> 13:11.830
Sky Boom-Boom.

333
13:12.160 --> 13:13.220
It's...

334
13:13.870 --> 13:15.190
Lightning mango!

335
13:16.570 --> 13:17.430
What even is that?

336
13:17.450 --> 13:19.390
There's no such mango variety, alright?

337
13:19.630 --> 13:20.360
Try again!

338
13:20.380 --> 13:21.790
Sky Boom-Boom.

339
13:24.120 --> 13:24.670
Oh.

340
13:24.690 --> 13:25.950
Falan mango, thunderous sky in Thai!

341
13:25.970 --> 13:26.540
Correct!

342
13:26.560 --> 13:27.160
- Whoa. - Oh.

343
13:27.180 --> 13:28.230
You got one right.

344
13:28.250 --> 13:30.490
What about these fibrous ones?

345
13:30.510 --> 13:31.070
That's plywood.

346
13:32.010 --> 13:32.720
Mangoes!

347
13:32.740 --> 13:34.510
- Plywood is made from wood fibers, though. - No, no.

348
13:34.550 --> 13:35.830
- That one? - Yes, yes.

349
13:35.890 --> 13:36.830
Here's a hint.

350
13:38.700 --> 13:39.230
Ooh...

351
13:39.450 --> 13:40.030
Oh?

352
13:40.260 --> 13:40.880
Captured?

353
13:41.910 --> 13:43.200
What do you mean, captured?

354
13:43.220 --> 13:44.150
Did the mango commit tax fraud?

355
13:44.670 --> 13:46.270
No. Watch again.

356
13:50.560 --> 13:51.760
Ooh!

357
13:52.390 --> 13:53.510
Sexy mango.

358
13:53.890 --> 13:54.610
Sexy mango.

359
13:54.630 --> 13:56.160
I've never had that before.

360
13:56.180 --> 13:57.030
We don't even have that.

361
13:57.230 --> 13:57.870
What?

362
13:58.050 --> 13:58.960
Watch closely.

363
14:02.790 --> 14:03.760
Ooh...

364
14:04.290 --> 14:05.710
With this squeeze...

365
14:05.900 --> 14:06.860
it has to be...

366
14:07.070 --> 14:08.110
Okrong mango, cleavage in Thai!

367
14:08.130 --> 14:09.490
- There! - Good job!

368
14:09.510 --> 14:10.960
You got two right.

369
14:11.070 --> 14:14.230
What about this nutty, crisp, and sour one?

370
14:14.250 --> 14:15.670
Hey handsome,

371
14:15.910 --> 14:16.830
wanna...

372
14:17.400 --> 14:18.950
have a one-night stand with me?

373
14:18.990 --> 14:19.750
Okay.

374
14:19.870 --> 14:20.540
- I'll go. - Let's go.

375
14:20.560 --> 14:21.850
- No, you're guessing the mango! - Oh, no?

376
14:21.870 --> 14:23.250
- Guess the mango. - I see.

377
14:24.500 --> 14:25.430
Handsome...

378
14:26.130 --> 14:27.110
This seductive...

379
14:28.600 --> 14:31.080
- Are you still thinking? - I am, I am.

380
14:32.780 --> 14:33.750
Rad mango, seductive ladies in Thai!

381
14:33.900 --> 14:34.630
That's right!

382
14:35.700 --> 14:36.990
- Good job! - What's Rad mango in English?

383
14:37.020 --> 14:37.550
In English?

384
14:37.570 --> 14:38.540
Char-rad-e mango.

385
14:38.560 --> 14:39.390
- Huh?! - Whoa?!

386
14:40.050 --> 14:41.350
- Take this. - Ow!

387
14:41.390 --> 14:43.060
You're a pro, huh?

388
14:43.360 --> 14:45.150
I'm gonna send you to live with Mom at the farm.

389
14:45.170 --> 14:46.020
I'm not going.

390
14:46.250 --> 14:48.630
Just so I can go back and hear them whisper that Mom only took me in?

391
14:49.000 --> 14:51.400
You and Mom look alike, but I look nothing like her.

392
14:53.930 --> 14:55.070
Aw...

393
14:55.090 --> 14:56.750
You may not look like her,

394
14:57.110 --> 14:58.630
but you look like Dad.

395
14:59.200 --> 15:00.260
Bulky,

396
15:00.360 --> 15:01.370
big and tall,

397
15:01.630 --> 15:03.850
with lots of muscle.

398
15:03.870 --> 15:05.510
I only see fat. Not muscle.

399
15:06.650 --> 15:07.270
He has muscle.

400
15:07.660 --> 15:08.670
It's just a bit hidden.

401
15:08.860 --> 15:10.110
Like inverted nipples.

402
15:10.130 --> 15:11.710
It's still there; you just can't see it.

403
15:11.730 --> 15:12.830
They fold inward...

404
15:12.850 --> 15:14.550
Don't explain anymore. It's disgusting.

405
15:14.570 --> 15:15.010
Really?

406
15:15.030 --> 15:16.510
You're comparing it to nipples? Are you crazy?

407
15:16.530 --> 15:17.380
Whoa...

408
15:17.540 --> 15:18.790
- Uh, Dolly? - Yes?

409
15:18.810 --> 15:20.050
The coffee is ready.

410
15:20.070 --> 15:21.310
Please deliver it for me.

411
15:22.200 --> 15:24.220
Rest assured, I'll take care of it.

412
15:24.690 --> 15:26.230
Mr. Drip's café is like my own.

413
15:26.600 --> 15:27.230
Huh?

414
15:28.100 --> 15:28.910
What do you mean, "Huh?"

415
15:29.380 --> 15:30.070
Well...

416
15:30.160 --> 15:32.030
we're neighbors.

417
15:32.130 --> 15:32.950
We should help each other out.

418
15:32.980 --> 15:34.290
Well, well, well...

419
15:34.310 --> 15:37.250
When Auntie Duang asks you to deliver food, you always drag your feet.

420
15:37.280 --> 15:38.430
But now, look how eager you are.

421
15:38.930 --> 15:39.990
Come on, now.

422
15:40.250 --> 15:41.160
I'll get going.

423
15:41.180 --> 15:42.430
We can talk about the mangoes later.

424
15:42.810 --> 15:43.340
Oh, Dolly.

425
15:43.360 --> 15:44.430
Oh, Dawin.

426
15:46.390 --> 15:47.380
Oh, hey, Mr. Dawin.

427
15:47.530 --> 15:48.810
You're here for the mangoes, right?

428
15:48.830 --> 15:50.870
- That's right. - I've got that ready for you over there.

429
15:50.890 --> 15:52.190
- Thank you. - My pleasure.

430
15:55.170 --> 15:56.670
Where's my chili salt dip?

431
15:56.810 --> 15:58.110
Oh...

432
15:58.510 --> 15:59.730
darn it, Mom.

433
15:59.750 --> 16:02.110
At her age, she often forgets things.

434
16:02.170 --> 16:03.170
She probably forgot to make some for you.

435
16:03.190 --> 16:03.670
It's alright.

436
16:03.690 --> 16:05.910
Daeng, give him some of ours.

437
16:09.640 --> 16:10.550
No way.

438
16:10.870 --> 16:11.790
It's mine.

439
16:11.900 --> 16:13.830
He's our mom's customer. Be nice.

440
16:14.910 --> 16:16.200
Don't be difficult.

441
16:16.220 --> 16:17.300
Share a little, will you?

442
16:18.650 --> 16:19.880
May I have a cup?

443
16:19.900 --> 16:20.830
Oh, of course.

444
16:22.270 --> 16:22.940
Here.

445
16:23.610 --> 16:24.270
Share some.

446
16:24.430 --> 16:25.190
Pour it in.

447
16:25.210 --> 16:26.360
Ugh, we've got plenty.

448
16:26.380 --> 16:27.350
This is enough.

449
16:28.050 --> 16:29.430
Hey, why so stingy?

450
16:31.540 --> 16:32.420
- Whoa! - Ow!

451
16:34.070 --> 16:35.470
My eyes!

452
16:35.490 --> 16:37.030
Whoa, I'm sorry. I didn't mean to.

453
16:37.070 --> 16:39.070
- Tissues, tissues. - Ow, my eyes!

454
16:39.110 --> 16:40.590
I can't take it anymore.

455
16:40.630 --> 16:41.150
Where is it?

456
16:41.170 --> 16:42.160
Hey, are you okay?

457
16:42.810 --> 16:45.060
- Ugh, he's over there! - Oh, whoa!

458
16:45.180 --> 16:46.510
Hey, go check on him.

459
16:46.670 --> 16:47.610
Oh!

460
16:47.630 --> 16:48.510
Don't crowd around him.

461
16:48.870 --> 16:49.650
Give him some space!

462
16:49.670 --> 16:51.150
- There's no one there. - Gently, gently.

463
16:51.550 --> 16:52.910
- Ow. - Get him to a doctor.

464
16:52.960 --> 16:54.010
- Doctor, doctor. - Go, go, go!

465
16:54.030 --> 16:55.680
- Go see a doctor. - Come on, go.

466
16:55.700 --> 16:56.170
Go, go, go.

467
16:56.190 --> 16:58.060
- Help. I can't see. - Alright, go, go.

468
16:58.080 --> 16:59.580
- Ow. - Let's go, let's go.

469
17:00.270 --> 17:02.230
We're in the same line of work.

470
17:02.250 --> 17:04.869
I know that when you have to memorize your lines or...

471
17:05.180 --> 17:07.310
get into character, you need to concentrate.

472
17:07.990 --> 17:08.750
By the way...

473
17:08.890 --> 17:11.470
What movie are you rehearsing for right now?

474
17:11.829 --> 17:13.359
I can be your acting partner.

475
17:14.069 --> 17:15.430
Whether you need a som tum vendor...

476
17:17.069 --> 17:18.230
Delish som tum

477
17:18.430 --> 17:20.310
right this way!

478
17:20.329 --> 17:21.310
This way!

479
17:21.410 --> 17:22.390
Or a cop.

480
17:23.810 --> 17:24.510
Drop your weapon.

481
17:24.970 --> 17:25.829
Put your hands up.

482
17:27.910 --> 17:29.110
Or maybe a midwife.

483
17:34.190 --> 17:35.270
Push, Nak.

484
17:39.790 --> 17:40.590
Mak,

485
17:40.610 --> 17:42.230
help me...

486
17:43.060 --> 17:43.990
Ugh!

487
17:44.100 --> 17:45.190
You can stop now.

488
17:45.980 --> 17:47.390
If you really want to help me out,

489
17:47.490 --> 17:48.160
go.

490
17:48.950 --> 17:51.350
Lie down and stay still, like a dead body.

491
17:52.960 --> 17:53.590
Huh?

492
18:00.420 --> 18:01.360
Go, go.

493
18:01.810 --> 18:03.320
- No, not that. No. - Huh?

494
18:03.340 --> 18:03.850
What do you mean, no?

495
18:03.870 --> 18:05.410
That isn't a white cane, that's my baton.

496
18:05.430 --> 18:06.190
Your cane is here.

497
18:06.830 --> 18:07.830
Stop knocking on it already.

498
18:08.560 --> 18:09.130
This way.

499
18:09.150 --> 18:09.870
Careful.

500
18:11.770 --> 18:14.560
With his customer getting blinded like this,

501
18:14.710 --> 18:17.540
has Mr. Drip even checked the feng shui of his cafe?

502
18:17.560 --> 18:18.580
I'm not blind yet.

503
18:19.610 --> 18:20.270
This way.

504
18:20.970 --> 18:22.070
Who talks to coffee beans?

505
18:23.250 --> 18:24.160
I'm not blind yet.

506
18:24.510 --> 18:25.790
The doctor said my eyes are inflamed,

507
18:25.810 --> 18:27.430
so I have to wear eye shields temporarily.

508
18:29.730 --> 18:33.790
Poor thing...

509
18:33.900 --> 18:35.470
Even if you're not blind, it's practically the same thing.

510
18:35.590 --> 18:38.690
Someone who once lived in a world of light

511
18:38.710 --> 18:40.030
now has to live in darkness.

512
18:40.590 --> 18:42.230
Even walking has become difficult.

513
18:42.310 --> 18:45.190
Oh, and your room is on the fourth floor...

514
18:45.210 --> 18:47.110
You poor soul.

515
18:48.580 --> 18:50.830
I'll just chalk it up to my own bad luck, Guard Dum.

516
18:50.990 --> 18:51.610
Yes...

517
18:52.130 --> 18:53.390
Thank you for worrying about me.

518
18:53.410 --> 18:55.150
It's alright. I hope you get well soon.

519
18:55.710 --> 18:57.050
No, he's that way.

520
18:58.330 --> 18:59.200
This way. Here.

521
18:59.220 --> 18:59.550
Ugh.

522
18:59.570 --> 19:00.990
If you can't see, just stay still.

523
19:01.250 --> 19:04.030
If it's that difficult, why not go back to the hospital?

524
19:06.470 --> 19:08.510
I can't afford a hospital room.

525
19:08.670 --> 19:09.380
Ugh.

526
19:09.570 --> 19:10.550
There's no need for him to do that.

527
19:10.670 --> 19:11.710
You have to take care of him.

528
19:11.750 --> 19:12.260
Huh?

529
19:12.300 --> 19:13.830
What are you confused about? You hurt his eyes.

530
19:13.850 --> 19:14.710
You have to take responsibility.

531
19:15.310 --> 19:17.110
Listen, from now on...

532
19:17.690 --> 19:20.350
you have to be his eyes until he recovers.

533
19:21.110 --> 19:22.070
No way!

534
19:23.190 --> 19:24.030
I got chills.

535
19:24.490 --> 19:26.030
If I have to take care of him,

536
19:26.180 --> 19:28.070
I'd rather hire a caregiver.

537
19:29.370 --> 19:30.310
Your medicine is right here.

538
19:30.330 --> 19:30.830
What?

539
19:30.850 --> 19:32.190
Hey, that's a waste of money.

540
19:33.510 --> 19:34.430
He's blind, though.

541
19:37.360 --> 19:38.570
- Guard Dum! - Oh...

542
19:38.590 --> 19:41.190
I thought you said this would make your brother hold my hand?

543
19:42.160 --> 19:42.830
Huh?

544
19:42.850 --> 19:44.590
Mr. Dawin, you can see?

545
19:46.310 --> 19:47.550
Don't tell Handyman Daeng about this.

546
19:47.570 --> 19:49.580
I just wanted an excuse to hold his hand

547
19:49.750 --> 19:51.030
and talk to Gramps' ghost.

548
19:51.330 --> 19:52.290
Don't tell anyone.

549
19:52.310 --> 19:53.070
What now?

550
19:54.160 --> 19:55.750
I forgot how heartless he can be.

551
19:58.620 --> 19:59.620
No wonder...

552
19:59.910 --> 20:01.580
he kept pushing us together.

553
20:02.150 --> 20:04.670
This time...you won't just see ghosts.

554
20:04.960 --> 20:07.130
You'll come face-to-face with the Grim Reaper.

555
20:13.530 --> 20:14.560
Let me check the number real quick...

556
20:14.890 --> 20:15.590
It's the right one, though.

557
20:18.450 --> 20:19.230
- What? - Huh?

558
20:19.980 --> 20:23.620
Room 407's listed number isn't going through.

559
20:23.930 --> 20:24.970
Did he put in a fake number?

560
20:24.990 --> 20:26.070
How would I know?

561
20:27.180 --> 20:27.980
Ms. Danis!

562
20:28.540 --> 20:29.250
Ms. Danis?

563
20:29.270 --> 20:31.110
Dennis isn't around. She stepped out.

564
20:31.170 --> 20:32.100
Is something up?

565
20:32.260 --> 20:32.890
Where did she go?

566
20:32.910 --> 20:33.230
Oh!

567
20:33.250 --> 20:33.760
Oh!

568
20:34.410 --> 20:36.160
Are you dressing up as an oil-seeping pillar?

569
20:36.660 --> 20:37.340
Both yantra cloth

570
20:37.360 --> 20:38.410
and three-colored cloth.

571
20:39.030 --> 20:39.910
Auntie Duang, what are you doing?

572
20:39.930 --> 20:41.160
I'm not dressing up as anything.

573
20:41.180 --> 20:42.870
These are sacred items.

574
20:43.710 --> 20:45.360
Dollar told me

575
20:45.380 --> 20:48.140
the killer is still lurking around this dorm,

576
20:48.160 --> 20:49.030
so I'm keeping these close

577
20:49.230 --> 20:50.750
for protection.

578
20:51.910 --> 20:53.330
If I were the killer,

579
20:53.350 --> 20:55.640
I would not approach her.

580
20:55.660 --> 20:57.190
She is definitely crazy.

581
20:57.950 --> 20:58.800
- Oh. - Hm?

582
20:58.820 --> 21:00.710
Have you talked to the tenant in Room 407 yet?

583
21:00.820 --> 21:02.100
I haven't, Auntie Duang.

584
21:02.190 --> 21:04.170
I'm waiting for Dax so we can go together.

585
21:04.190 --> 21:05.250
Want me to take you there?

586
21:05.270 --> 21:06.270
I think he's home.

587
21:06.510 --> 21:08.540
He called me to order food this morning.

588
21:08.560 --> 21:10.410
I left the food at his door.

589
21:10.710 --> 21:12.110
You can try your luck.

590
21:12.160 --> 21:13.510
One crazy person versus another.

591
21:13.710 --> 21:15.310
They might just balance each other out.

592
21:16.390 --> 21:16.960
Let's go.

593
21:17.270 --> 21:18.140
It's alright, Auntie Duang.

594
21:18.290 --> 21:19.110
I'll handle it.

595
21:19.130 --> 21:20.840
Mom, Mom. Mom!

596
21:20.860 --> 21:22.020
- Ugh, Dolly, - Mom!

597
21:22.040 --> 21:23.180
why are you making a fuss?!

598
21:23.200 --> 21:24.050
This is bad, Mom!

599
21:24.070 --> 21:26.070
Dollar sent me a photo of the killer.

600
21:26.090 --> 21:27.120
Really? Where?

601
21:27.140 --> 21:27.710
Here.

602
21:27.800 --> 21:28.310
Oh?

603
21:31.120 --> 21:32.700
Crunchy boy is the killer?

604
21:34.570 --> 21:35.950
Wrong one. Not this one.

605
21:38.720 --> 21:39.540
Whoa...

606
21:39.560 --> 21:41.070
Why do you have so many photos of the crunchy boy?

607
21:41.690 --> 21:43.090
- Uh... - For the ordination hall walls?

608
21:43.880 --> 21:45.770
These are just references for my costumes.

609
21:45.790 --> 21:46.670
Yeah, yeah.

610
21:46.870 --> 21:47.750
Come on, let me see.

611
21:47.780 --> 21:48.750
Here.

612
21:48.820 --> 21:49.710
This is the real killer.

613
21:50.000 --> 21:50.560
Oh?

614
21:50.580 --> 21:52.470
He looks just like the tenant from Room 407.

615
21:52.580 --> 21:54.190
Right? I feel like I've seen him before, too.

616
21:54.490 --> 21:55.250
No, not really.

617
21:55.270 --> 21:58.070
That is him. The bag looks just like his.

618
21:59.300 --> 21:59.710
Oh.

619
22:01.050 --> 22:01.820
Dax texted me.

620
22:01.840 --> 22:02.340
Huh?

621
22:02.640 --> 22:05.340
Dobby, I'm with the tenant from Room 407.

622
22:05.610 --> 22:07.990
"Don't worry, I'll handle it."

623
22:08.170 --> 22:09.050
- Huh?! - Huh?!

624
22:09.380 --> 22:11.150
Is Mr. Dax in the room with the killer?

625
22:11.180 --> 22:11.800
Oh, no...

626
22:12.220 --> 22:13.510
Dobby, call him.

627
22:13.700 --> 22:14.970
Tell him to run. Hurry!

628
22:16.720 --> 22:18.110
I put my phone on airplane mode, like you asked.

629
22:19.050 --> 22:20.930
That way, no one will interrupt us

630
22:20.950 --> 22:22.070
while we're rehearsing.

631
22:27.880 --> 22:28.620
Can you reach him?

632
22:28.640 --> 22:29.490
He's not answering.

633
22:30.200 --> 22:31.110
He turned his phone off.

634
22:31.130 --> 22:32.310
Maybe he's in danger.

635
22:34.280 --> 22:34.830
How about this?

636
22:34.870 --> 22:37.560
Dolly, tell Dollar to bring the police here right now.

637
22:37.580 --> 22:38.990
- Right now, come on. - Hey!

638
22:39.380 --> 22:41.470
Dax will be dead before the police show up.

639
22:41.490 --> 22:42.110
Yeah.

640
22:42.690 --> 22:43.980
Then I'll go help him.

641
22:44.000 --> 22:44.710
- Yeah! - Yeah!

642
22:44.730 --> 22:46.060
Bring the police up the second they get here.

643
22:46.080 --> 22:46.640
Okay.

644
22:46.660 --> 22:47.470
- Alright. - Hurry.

645
22:47.620 --> 22:48.070
Hey.

646
22:48.520 --> 22:49.590
Hurry up!

647
22:51.930 --> 22:53.320
Oh, you're here already?

648
22:53.730 --> 22:54.940
What you did was wrong.

649
22:54.960 --> 22:57.940
You can't hire someone else to take care of Mr. Dawin.

650
22:57.990 --> 23:00.250
You hurt him, so you have to take care of him yourself.

651
23:00.270 --> 23:01.980
You can't trust anyone these days.

652
23:02.000 --> 23:04.190
What if they stab Mr. Dawin when you're not around?

653
23:04.230 --> 23:05.200
Stabby-stab.

654
23:05.220 --> 23:05.630
What will you do?

655
23:05.650 --> 23:06.590
What if they have a gun?

656
23:06.610 --> 23:08.230
He'll get shot. Bang, bang, bang.

657
23:08.290 --> 23:09.350
What if there's a knife attached to the gun?

658
23:09.720 --> 23:10.250
Stab.

659
23:10.270 --> 23:10.870
Bang!

660
23:10.920 --> 23:11.310
Stab.

661
23:11.350 --> 23:11.870
Bang!

662
23:11.890 --> 23:12.350
Stab.

663
23:12.370 --> 23:12.830
Bang!

664
23:12.850 --> 23:13.120
Stab.

665
23:13.140 --> 23:14.270
- Ugh! - Ugh!

666
23:14.310 --> 23:16.070
He's like Swiss cheese at this point. Put this away.

667
23:16.990 --> 23:17.940
Right in the eye!

668
23:19.020 --> 23:20.830
If you're going to hire someone to take care of me,

669
23:21.170 --> 23:22.070
I'll have to turn that down.

670
23:22.170 --> 23:23.610
I'm not comfortable with strangers.

671
23:23.630 --> 23:24.990
I'll take care of you.

672
23:26.350 --> 23:27.370
You sure change your mind fast.

673
23:27.590 --> 23:30.550
When I stepped outside, I realized

674
23:30.580 --> 23:33.470
I'd injured Mr. Dawin,

675
23:34.490 --> 23:37.150
so I thought it was best to take responsibility.

676
23:37.830 --> 23:40.430
To prove that to you,

677
23:40.450 --> 23:43.070
I bought these steamed buns for you.

678
23:45.350 --> 23:45.880
Ow.

679
23:45.900 --> 23:48.380
Hot, hot, hot!

680
23:48.430 --> 23:49.550
It's hot.

681
23:50.220 --> 23:52.430
Po, shush.

682
23:52.550 --> 23:56.950
Didn't I say I'd take care of Mr. Dawin?

683
24:00.800 --> 24:02.750
The steamed bun is still hot, though.

684
24:02.870 --> 24:04.930
Let me cool it down first.

685
24:08.390 --> 24:09.710
Whoa...

686
24:10.820 --> 24:12.510
Alright,

687
24:12.710 --> 24:13.350
It's not as hot now.

688
24:13.510 --> 24:14.110
Go on.

689
24:14.420 --> 24:15.230
Mr. Dawin,

690
24:15.310 --> 24:16.830
open wide. I'll feed you.

691
24:18.150 --> 24:20.150
I'm...not hungry yet.

692
24:22.100 --> 24:22.990
What?

693
24:23.100 --> 24:25.020
This is just a small steamed bun.

694
24:25.040 --> 24:27.750
Or maybe you don't want me to take care of you anymore?

695
24:30.300 --> 24:31.580
Uh...

696
24:32.220 --> 24:33.310
I'll eat it myself.

697
24:34.310 --> 24:36.910
It's a little embarrassing having you feed me.

698
24:37.020 --> 24:38.390
Oh...

699
24:38.700 --> 24:39.590
Alright, then.

700
24:42.090 --> 24:43.030
Oh...

701
24:43.290 --> 24:43.990
Uh...

702
24:44.350 --> 24:45.270
Oops!

703
24:45.320 --> 24:46.020
Oh...

704
24:46.320 --> 24:47.300
I'm sorry.

705
24:47.820 --> 24:49.270
I dropped it.

706
24:49.290 --> 24:51.270
- Oh, such a shame. - Oh.

707
24:51.690 --> 24:52.950
He can't eat it anymore.

708
24:53.040 --> 24:53.870
It's okay.

709
24:54.560 --> 24:56.300
I'll get you a new one.

710
24:56.490 --> 24:57.190
Phew...

711
25:07.790 --> 25:08.630
Oh, wow...

712
25:11.320 --> 25:12.230
So cruel.

713
25:19.480 --> 25:20.180
It's not hot anymore.

714
25:20.200 --> 25:20.960
Hey...

715
25:20.980 --> 25:22.350
Alright, open wide.

716
25:23.120 --> 25:24.390
Uh... Okay.

717
25:32.490 --> 25:34.030
He only had to fake an eye infection at first.

718
25:34.190 --> 25:36.950
But at this rate, he'll be fighting demons on the toilet.

719
25:38.870 --> 25:41.430
I think Daeng already knows we lied to him.

720
25:41.780 --> 25:43.150
- Let's make a run for it. - Yeah.

721
25:43.900 --> 25:45.510
Where do you think you're going, Po?

722
25:46.730 --> 25:49.290
Stay and help me coax Mr. Dawin into eating first.

723
25:50.350 --> 25:53.550
He seems suspicious of me whenever I try to take care of him, right?

724
25:54.480 --> 25:54.920
Uh...

725
25:56.170 --> 25:59.310
Then I suppose I can't take care of you anymore.

726
26:01.540 --> 26:02.190
Wait!

727
26:03.460 --> 26:05.670
I'm not suspicious of you taking care of me at all.

728
26:09.570 --> 26:10.790
Then eat.

729
26:14.860 --> 26:17.270
No one will ever find out that I'm the killer.

730
26:18.390 --> 26:20.910
You'll take this secret to your grave.

731
26:24.280 --> 26:24.910
Wait.

732
26:25.760 --> 26:28.150
This line in the script is too short.

733
26:28.460 --> 26:31.430
I can't quite tell what kind of fear this character is experiencing.

734
26:31.600 --> 26:32.950
Ugh...

735
26:33.320 --> 26:35.020
You can act however you want.

736
26:35.040 --> 26:36.910
You'll die after one stab anyway.

737
26:37.860 --> 26:38.590
That won't do.

738
26:39.200 --> 26:41.200
We need to understand the character's emotions

739
26:41.220 --> 26:42.990
to know how to portray them.

740
26:43.100 --> 26:44.110
Maybe he's really scared.

741
26:44.180 --> 26:47.390
No. Hey...don't come any closer.

742
26:47.750 --> 26:49.710
Or maybe it's resentment.

743
26:50.780 --> 26:52.190
If you kill me...

744
26:52.540 --> 26:54.750
I'll come back as a ghost and break your neck.

745
26:56.230 --> 26:57.990
Or is it Uno Laothong's fear?

746
26:58.680 --> 27:01.700
I can't. I can't with this house. It's too scary.

747
27:02.350 --> 27:04.320
I don't want to be here any longer.

748
27:04.340 --> 27:05.310
I don't want to be here either...

749
27:05.960 --> 27:06.660
Pardon?

750
27:06.960 --> 27:07.640
Oh.

751
27:08.160 --> 27:09.040
I think...

752
27:09.580 --> 27:10.630
we should move on to the next scene.

753
27:10.680 --> 27:12.110
Let's move on from being threatened...

754
27:12.270 --> 27:13.390
to the chase scene.

755
27:13.790 --> 27:15.110
Let's go full send.

756
27:15.140 --> 27:15.910
By the way...

757
27:16.270 --> 27:17.830
how would he be feeling as he runs away?

758
27:18.090 --> 27:18.710
Huh?

759
27:20.880 --> 27:22.230
Is he running away in fear?

760
27:26.080 --> 27:27.950
Or is he paranoid?

761
27:29.240 --> 27:30.320
Don't follow me.

762
27:31.290 --> 27:32.270
Don't follow me!

763
27:34.550 --> 27:36.510
Or maybe like Toon Artiwara.

764
27:37.470 --> 27:39.510
I want Thai people to be healthy!

765
27:41.620 --> 27:42.350
Which is it?

766
27:42.740 --> 27:44.070
Run however you want.

767
27:44.240 --> 27:45.120
Just run.

768
27:45.560 --> 27:47.210
Run out of the room. Go on.

769
27:47.230 --> 27:47.990
Run.

770
27:48.720 --> 27:49.700
Don't kill me!

771
27:49.720 --> 27:50.990
Don't... Don't kill me.

772
27:51.100 --> 27:53.350
Don't kill me!

773
27:53.670 --> 27:54.630
Don't kill me...

774
27:54.710 --> 27:56.190
Ugh...

775
27:56.490 --> 27:57.750
Just kill me already.

776
27:58.510 --> 28:00.550
[The D Dorm]

777
28:04.520 --> 28:05.640
Do not tell me...

778
28:05.820 --> 28:07.710
Dax is dead dead?

779
28:09.300 --> 28:10.550
How could you say that?

780
28:10.700 --> 28:11.960
That's my friend, Grandpa.

781
28:14.490 --> 28:15.690
I'm here to help.

782
28:16.990 --> 28:17.990
Oh?

783
28:19.160 --> 28:20.830
What are you wearing, Mr. Dolly?

784
28:21.460 --> 28:22.600
I wanted to help,

785
28:22.620 --> 28:23.490
but Mom was worried about me,

786
28:23.510 --> 28:25.510
so she made me wear these things for protection.

787
28:26.310 --> 28:27.320
Come on, now...

788
28:27.690 --> 28:28.520
Here!

789
28:29.120 --> 28:30.630
Mom told me to give you this.

790
28:30.960 --> 28:31.940
For me?

791
28:36.090 --> 28:37.040
What?

792
28:47.710 --> 28:48.670
Dax.

793
28:48.950 --> 28:50.160
Whoa...

794
28:56.750 --> 28:57.310
Oh!

795
28:58.220 --> 29:01.510
Dax is dead dead!

796
29:02.340 --> 29:03.350
Dax...

797
29:06.040 --> 29:07.790
It's gonna be okay, Mr. Dobby.

798
29:07.940 --> 29:08.680
Wow.

799
29:08.700 --> 29:10.150
That was amazing, Mr. Disney.

800
29:10.460 --> 29:13.290
The moment you checked to see if I was still breathing...

801
29:13.500 --> 29:14.060
Wow...

802
29:14.080 --> 29:16.160
Your eyes and that grin make you look like

803
29:16.580 --> 29:18.610
a killer who's actually trying to murder me.

804
29:18.630 --> 29:20.720
If I wanted to kill you, I would've done it the moment you said...

805
29:20.740 --> 29:22.870
"I can't with this house. It's too scary."

806
29:25.350 --> 29:25.870
You know?!

807
29:26.010 --> 29:26.750
Huh?

808
29:27.340 --> 29:28.370
Oh, I mean,

809
29:28.390 --> 29:30.190
your acting was so good.

810
29:30.520 --> 29:32.330
You frustrated me so much that

811
29:32.350 --> 29:34.770
I really felt like killing you, Mr. Dax.

812
29:34.790 --> 29:35.510
Wow.

813
29:38.270 --> 29:39.140
What's the matter?

814
29:39.640 --> 29:40.390
I'm flattered.

815
29:40.510 --> 29:43.350
Getting a compliment from my beloved superstar

816
29:43.440 --> 29:44.630
really made my day.

817
29:45.240 --> 29:46.990
By the way, which scene should we do next?

818
29:47.400 --> 29:48.430
Let's go with...

819
29:48.560 --> 29:49.510
the dismemberment part.

820
29:49.920 --> 29:52.150
I want to practice the movements.

821
29:52.170 --> 29:52.870
Alright.

822
29:52.970 --> 29:54.470
What kind of corpse would you like?

823
29:55.070 --> 29:57.500
A fresh, still-twitching corpse?

824
30:02.490 --> 30:03.110
Or...

825
30:03.310 --> 30:05.180
a long-dead, bloated corpse?

826
30:08.200 --> 30:09.180
Which do you prefer?

827
30:11.680 --> 30:13.310
Stay still like a corpse would.

828
30:14.040 --> 30:15.060
Leave that to me.

829
30:17.360 --> 30:20.140
Why do I have to go in there?

830
30:20.160 --> 30:20.930
I do not want to go inside.

831
30:20.950 --> 30:22.430
I am scared of ghosts.

832
30:22.590 --> 30:24.930
Grandpa, you're a ghost. Why are you even scared of ghosts?

833
30:24.950 --> 30:27.690
Ghosts can be scared of ghosts, too.

834
30:28.300 --> 30:30.340
I do not want to see anything gory.

835
30:30.360 --> 30:31.750
Grandpa...

836
30:36.230 --> 30:37.640
You are worried about your friend, right?

837
30:37.660 --> 30:38.490
Yes!

838
30:39.220 --> 30:39.690
Fine.

839
30:40.000 --> 30:40.890
I will go in there.

840
30:41.350 --> 30:42.660
Let me close my eyes first.

841
30:52.230 --> 30:53.310
What are you doing to Dax?

842
30:58.320 --> 30:59.160
Is that blood...?

843
31:07.710 --> 31:08.640
I cannot take it anymore.

844
31:20.440 --> 31:21.070
Wow.

845
31:21.400 --> 31:22.310
How was it?

846
31:22.960 --> 31:24.230
Is it as realistic as you wanted it to be?

847
31:24.870 --> 31:26.940
Using sauce as blood

848
31:26.960 --> 31:28.690
really helps build the emotion, huh?

849
31:28.710 --> 31:30.270
Now I understand...

850
31:30.290 --> 31:32.950
the thrill psycho killers feel when dismembering a body.

851
31:33.000 --> 31:35.870
I told you I'm a professional supporting actor.

852
31:35.890 --> 31:38.270
I have a bunch of other tricks to share with you.

853
31:39.160 --> 31:40.140
Please share them.

854
31:40.520 --> 31:43.140
You really helped me out today.

855
31:44.080 --> 31:45.960
Oh, I've got a concert coming up.

856
31:46.080 --> 31:49.310
I'll save a seat just for you, then.

857
31:49.740 --> 31:50.220
Yes!

858
31:50.240 --> 31:51.870
Oh, thank you so much.

859
31:52.320 --> 31:54.030
I have to practice my dance moves now.

860
31:54.320 --> 31:55.350
Thank you.

861
31:56.000 --> 31:56.940
I'll go clean up first.

862
32:22.440 --> 32:23.590
This tastes good.

863
32:24.510 --> 32:27.430
He really is a psycho killer.

864
32:31.110 --> 32:31.830
Ugh.

865
32:32.340 --> 32:34.080
Where did Dax go?

866
32:37.390 --> 32:38.830
Do not tell me...

867
32:38.990 --> 32:40.140
That suitc...

868
32:40.890 --> 32:44.030
I cannot stay here any longer!

869
32:52.310 --> 32:53.510
- So? - Dobby!

870
32:53.890 --> 32:54.680
Dax...

871
32:54.930 --> 32:56.510
Dax is dead!

872
32:57.320 --> 32:59.960
He was chopped up into bite-sized pieces

873
32:59.990 --> 33:01.510
and shoved into a suitcase!

874
33:02.310 --> 33:04.150
Dax is dead!

875
33:04.260 --> 33:06.090
- Dax is dead, Grandpa? - Yeah.

876
33:06.150 --> 33:07.860
Mr. Dobby... Mr. Dobby!

877
33:08.030 --> 33:08.940
Mr. Dobby!

878
33:09.130 --> 33:11.130
Mr. Dobby. Mr. Dobby.

879
33:11.490 --> 33:12.300
Mr. Dobby.

880
33:14.870 --> 33:16.010
What's wrong, Mr. Dobby?

881
33:18.210 --> 33:19.580
I talked to Dollar.

882
33:19.900 --> 33:21.900
He said that the police are on their way.

883
33:22.240 --> 33:23.250
He told us to hang on a second.

884
33:23.270 --> 33:24.550
- Hang on? - Yes.

885
33:24.990 --> 33:25.790
I still have to?

886
33:26.640 --> 33:27.630
I'm not gonna wait anymore!

887
33:27.650 --> 33:28.850
Whoa!

888
33:30.800 --> 33:31.430
What?

889
33:31.990 --> 33:33.010
Who are you?

890
33:33.030 --> 33:33.990
Why did you come in here?

891
33:37.250 --> 33:38.910
Shut up, you murderer!

892
33:38.950 --> 33:39.870
What murderer...?

893
33:40.590 --> 33:41.520
Mr. Dobby, be careful!

894
33:42.450 --> 33:43.030
Don't move...

895
33:45.390 --> 33:46.030
Dobby.

896
33:46.070 --> 33:47.270
Dax...

897
33:47.900 --> 33:49.350
is in that suitcase.

898
33:50.590 --> 33:51.850
Why did you kill my friend?

899
33:51.870 --> 33:55.750
♫I love you so, so much♫

900
33:55.880 --> 33:57.380
I didn't kill...

901
33:57.400 --> 33:58.910
You're still lying, huh?!

902
33:59.350 --> 34:01.830
You killed him and shoved him into that suitcase, didn't you?!

903
34:01.850 --> 34:02.490
There!

904
34:02.510 --> 34:09.030
♫Cutie pie, I only think of you♫

905
34:09.080 --> 34:10.260
Ow...

906
34:12.260 --> 34:13.250
Are you gonna grab the knife?!

907
34:14.120 --> 34:15.230
You are, aren't you?

908
34:15.260 --> 34:16.790
Not dead...

909
34:16.850 --> 34:17.790
Fine, then...

910
34:17.830 --> 34:19.070
die!

911
34:19.100 --> 34:21.570
♫I want to tell you, I want to embrace you♫

912
34:21.590 --> 34:23.750
♫You cutie pie♫

913
34:23.880 --> 34:24.870
How does that feel?!

914
34:26.590 --> 34:27.449
Dax...

915
34:27.469 --> 34:28.389
Dax...

916
34:28.699 --> 34:29.739
Dax...

917
34:30.320 --> 34:32.739
How am I gonna tell your parents about this?

918
34:33.280 --> 34:34.630
Dax, I'm sorry...

919
34:35.000 --> 34:39.150
♫I love you the way you are, my cutie pie♫

920
34:39.650 --> 34:41.480
My supporting actor.

921
34:41.500 --> 34:42.550
Dax!

922
34:43.820 --> 34:44.940
Dax.

923
34:46.040 --> 34:46.909
Dax...

924
34:48.280 --> 34:49.540
Dax...

925
34:49.760 --> 34:50.630
Why are you calling my name?

926
34:55.679 --> 34:56.449
Huh?

927
34:57.650 --> 34:58.550
He is still alive?

928
34:58.850 --> 34:59.470
Dax?

929
34:59.490 --> 35:00.470
You're still alive?

930
35:00.790 --> 35:01.670
What are you saying?

931
35:05.280 --> 35:06.150
Mr. Disney?!

932
35:06.840 --> 35:07.580
- Huh? - Huh?

933
35:07.600 --> 35:08.710
- Disney?! - Mr. Disney?

934
35:08.750 --> 35:09.630
Disney who?

935
35:09.650 --> 35:10.910
Disney, you know?

936
35:18.890 --> 35:19.630
He's...

937
35:19.660 --> 35:23.350
Mr. Disney, the five-time winner of the People's Choice Award!

938
35:25.510 --> 35:27.110
I punched him five times...

939
35:27.830 --> 35:28.720
Hey, Mr. Disney...

940
35:28.740 --> 35:29.910
Mr. Disney...

941
35:30.830 --> 35:34.630
The beloved superstar sure took a beating.

942
35:38.820 --> 35:39.910
When will you eat?

943
35:40.650 --> 35:41.790
Your eyes are better now, aren't they?

944
35:43.460 --> 35:43.960
Just.

945
35:43.990 --> 35:44.570
Give.

946
35:44.600 --> 35:45.190
Up.

947
35:45.400 --> 35:48.320
If you're gonna cough like that, you might as well just go tell him.

948
35:48.800 --> 35:49.760
If I eat it,

949
35:50.060 --> 35:51.940
can you promise you'll stay with me?

950
35:53.580 --> 35:54.800
You'll hold my hand

951
35:55.420 --> 35:56.860
wherever I want to go.

952
35:56.880 --> 35:57.650
Alright.

953
35:58.340 --> 35:59.680
I promise.

954
35:59.940 --> 36:00.710
Now eat!

955
36:09.350 --> 36:10.010
- Whoa! - What?!

956
36:10.030 --> 36:10.890
- Whoa! - Hey!

957
36:10.910 --> 36:12.350
Why did you eat it? Spit it out!

958
36:12.370 --> 36:13.110
You're gonna die!

959
36:14.100 --> 36:14.760
Spit it out!

960
36:15.380 --> 36:16.020
Spit it out!

961
36:16.850 --> 36:17.690
Not gonna spit it out, huh?

962
36:17.710 --> 36:18.790
Take this!

963
36:31.390 --> 36:32.270
Po,

964
36:32.560 --> 36:33.740
you traitor.

965
36:33.920 --> 36:35.590
You know full well I'm scared of ghosts.

966
36:35.610 --> 36:38.240
How dare you help him

967
36:38.450 --> 36:39.910
trick me into being his caretaker?

968
36:40.140 --> 36:40.950
Well...

969
36:41.160 --> 36:42.910
I already agreed to help him,

970
36:43.000 --> 36:44.910
so I have to keep my promise.

971
36:45.280 --> 36:47.990
Aren't you glad? Your little brother keeps his word.

972
36:49.620 --> 36:51.110
Didn't you say you'd get 2,000?

973
36:52.140 --> 36:53.230
- Shut it. - Oh.

974
36:54.620 --> 36:56.910
I did as you asked. I ate it.

975
36:57.030 --> 36:58.850
Now you have to keep your promise.

976
36:59.440 --> 37:01.150
You still have the nerve to ask me that?

977
37:01.380 --> 37:02.550
Seriously,

978
37:02.860 --> 37:03.990
what the hell is wrong with you?

979
37:04.400 --> 37:06.110
You're so obsessed with seeing ghosts.

980
37:07.250 --> 37:07.940
Or...

981
37:08.410 --> 37:10.480
you can't trick others by being a phony fortune teller anymore,

982
37:10.740 --> 37:12.510
so you've decided to be a shaman instead?

983
37:17.030 --> 37:18.070
I have my reasons.

984
37:18.180 --> 37:20.140
It doesn't matter why you did this.

985
37:20.450 --> 37:22.470
You can't go around harassing people like this.

986
37:23.710 --> 37:25.620
If you keep this up,

987
37:26.150 --> 37:28.590
I don't think we can share a dorm anymore.

988
37:44.660 --> 37:45.550
I want to see my mom!

989
37:50.310 --> 37:51.900
I want to see ghosts...

990
37:53.500 --> 37:54.830
because I want to see my mom.

991
37:57.940 --> 37:59.870
My mom passed away on the day I was born.

992
38:04.470 --> 38:07.020
Dad blamed me for her death, saying I was a jinx.

993
38:08.740 --> 38:10.580
My relatives also think I'm a jinx.

994
38:15.650 --> 38:17.310
Life has been pretty harsh on you,

995
38:18.560 --> 38:20.070
but I think they're right.

996
38:20.880 --> 38:22.450
See? Even when you're alone,

997
38:22.480 --> 38:24.050
you still manage to get into trouble.

998
38:24.680 --> 38:26.190
Stop talking.

999
38:26.440 --> 38:27.190
Give me your hand.

1000
38:27.210 --> 38:27.990
I don't want it.

1001
38:29.820 --> 38:31.270
I want to see her

1002
38:33.950 --> 38:35.580
and ask her...

1003
38:37.250 --> 38:39.350
if I was the one who killed her.

1004
38:43.270 --> 38:44.390
Are you done?

1005
38:45.650 --> 38:46.710
If you're done, leave.

1006
38:47.910 --> 38:48.750
Oh, wow...

1007
38:49.360 --> 38:50.120
Dang it, Daeng.

1008
38:50.340 --> 38:53.040
I never knew you could be so heartless.

1009
38:53.060 --> 38:54.910
His life is already hard enough. Why push him away?

1010
38:55.220 --> 38:56.070
You meanie!

1011
38:56.240 --> 38:56.790
Cruel!

1012
38:57.110 --> 38:57.630
Heartless!

1013
38:57.650 --> 38:58.510
Toxic!

1014
38:59.070 --> 39:01.250
♫You're toxic, I'm slippin'...♫

1015
39:01.620 --> 39:02.240
What's this?

1016
39:02.260 --> 39:03.000
The steamed bun from earlier.

1017
39:05.060 --> 39:06.580
If you don't want to help,

1018
39:07.830 --> 39:09.650
I won't bother you anymore.

1019
39:11.030 --> 39:11.590
Hey,

1020
39:12.680 --> 39:14.070
when did I say I wouldn't help?

1021
39:15.070 --> 39:16.390
Well, you told me to leave.

1022
39:20.700 --> 39:21.790
I meant, "Let's go,

1023
39:25.190 --> 39:26.550
let's look for your mother."

1024
39:27.800 --> 39:28.280
Hey...

1025
39:39.300 --> 39:40.850
But if we find your mom,

1026
39:41.520 --> 39:42.870
you'll have to talk to her yourself.

1027
39:43.790 --> 39:44.800
I'm scared of ghosts.

1028
39:46.600 --> 39:47.990
If you're scared of ghosts,

1029
39:48.860 --> 39:50.150
I'll cover your eyes.

1030
39:56.910 --> 39:57.650
Is this better?

1031
39:58.110 --> 39:58.960
Hey!

1032
39:58.980 --> 40:00.110
What are you doing?

1033
40:00.950 --> 40:02.110
Are you trying to blind me or something?

1034
40:03.040 --> 40:03.990
But you're scared of ghosts?

1035
40:04.740 --> 40:06.500
I can take care of myself.

1036
40:07.120 --> 40:08.510
If you want to see them, go ahead.

1037
40:16.990 --> 40:17.510
I'll give it my all.

1038
40:17.680 --> 40:19.590
Thank you for encouraging me.

1039
40:21.800 --> 40:22.590
I'm gonna cut your fingers off.

1040
40:22.660 --> 40:23.910
What encouragement? Give me 2,000.

1041
40:24.050 --> 40:25.120
Mm, that's right.

1042
40:25.890 --> 40:26.550
See?

1043
40:26.590 --> 40:27.410
Give him 500, too.

1044
40:27.430 --> 40:29.060
No, you still owe me 500.

1045
40:29.310 --> 40:30.630
- We're gonna share it. - Oh...

1046
40:35.640 --> 40:37.710
I'm so sorry, Mr. Disney.

1047
40:37.830 --> 40:40.910
I thought you were the dismemberment killer from the news.

1048
40:41.480 --> 40:42.470
It's alright.

1049
40:43.430 --> 40:45.390
It's partly my fault, too.

1050
40:45.650 --> 40:48.800
I was acting suspicious, and that made things worse.

1051
40:55.060 --> 40:55.710
Oh.

1052
40:56.590 --> 40:57.310
Whoa.

1053
40:57.650 --> 40:59.310
I'm really sorry, Mr. Disney.

1054
40:59.480 --> 41:00.550
Ugh...

1055
41:00.860 --> 41:01.840
I'm sorry.

1056
41:03.980 --> 41:04.850
By the way...

1057
41:05.180 --> 41:07.950
did you need something from the room owner?

1058
41:08.180 --> 41:08.790
Oh...

1059
41:09.500 --> 41:11.150
Can you take a look...

1060
41:11.560 --> 41:12.630
at this video?

1061
41:18.590 --> 41:20.270
Is this your manager?

1062
41:20.930 --> 41:22.270
No, this isn't my manager.

1063
41:22.440 --> 41:23.190
- Huh? - What?

1064
41:24.600 --> 41:25.510
That's me.

1065
41:25.540 --> 41:26.280
- Huh? - Huh?

1066
41:27.120 --> 41:28.590
I remember this box.

1067
41:28.980 --> 41:31.550
On that day, I came to put my things away.

1068
41:34.550 --> 41:35.470
We found him!

1069
41:35.510 --> 41:36.730
Finally...

1070
41:36.750 --> 41:39.750
I've found your relative, Gaysorn!

1071
41:43.140 --> 41:43.990
Mr. Disney,

1072
41:45.300 --> 41:46.890
do you have a relative...

1073
41:46.910 --> 41:47.910
named Gaysorn?

1074
41:49.740 --> 41:50.830
Gaysorn...

1075
41:59.470 --> 42:00.910
- No. - Oh.

1076
42:01.070 --> 42:01.950
No, huh...

1077
42:02.270 --> 42:04.230
Mr. Dax already asked me about this once.

1078
42:04.350 --> 42:06.710
I called my manager to ask them about this.

1079
42:07.480 --> 42:09.430
Oh, but they said...

1080
42:09.920 --> 42:10.550
Yeah?

1081
42:11.060 --> 42:11.710
What did they say?

1082
42:11.880 --> 42:13.870
They don't have any relatives named Gaysorn either.

1083
42:14.390 --> 42:15.790
- Why did he say "but," then? - Right?

1084
42:17.070 --> 42:17.740
Oh!

1085
42:18.360 --> 42:19.350
Mr. Disney,

1086
42:19.430 --> 42:20.650
the thing is...

1087
42:20.670 --> 42:23.310
the video was recorded on the day my grandpa passed away.

1088
42:23.600 --> 42:27.310
In the footage, you were walking up the stairs

1089
42:27.430 --> 42:29.350
when you dropped Grandma Gaysorn's photo.

1090
42:29.670 --> 42:31.030
Are you sure you're not her relative?

1091
42:31.140 --> 42:32.590
That photo isn't mine, though.

1092
42:32.820 --> 42:33.590
- What? - Huh?

1093
42:34.850 --> 42:36.830
It came falling down from upstairs.

1094
42:37.030 --> 42:38.150
Where did it come from, then?

1095
42:39.870 --> 42:40.670
Wait, wait, wait.

1096
42:42.050 --> 42:44.910
I think I know who dropped that photo.

1097
42:45.280 --> 42:46.990
On that day, I went up to the fourth floor

1098
42:47.140 --> 42:48.870
and saw a woman...

1099
42:48.950 --> 42:50.880
carrying a whole bunch of things.

1100
42:51.300 --> 42:53.230
I think she was the one who dropped the photo.

1101
42:55.060 --> 42:56.150
There's a female ghost in our dorm, too?

1102
42:56.300 --> 42:57.040
Hm?

1103
42:58.000 --> 42:59.000
I think she's human.

1104
42:59.030 --> 43:00.310
Just Grandpa's ghost is enough.

1105
43:02.600 --> 43:03.550
A woman...

1106
43:04.720 --> 43:05.460
Who?

1107
43:05.480 --> 43:07.600
I think she's the manager of this dorm.

1108
43:07.830 --> 43:08.950
Her name is Danis.

1109
43:09.190 --> 43:09.910
- Huh?! - Huh?!

1110
43:11.270 --> 43:12.270
Danis?

1111
43:12.820 --> 43:14.790
How could it be her?

1112
43:26.410 --> 43:28.920
Why is this ice cream seller dressed like that?

1113
43:29.120 --> 43:31.000
It is like he is from the Joseon era.

1114
43:36.300 --> 43:37.300
Delta,

1115
43:37.720 --> 43:38.560
do you remember me?

1116
43:38.580 --> 43:39.720
Dolly Darling?

1117
43:39.740 --> 43:40.720
Delta Oppa?

1118
43:40.740 --> 43:42.240
Hey, I thought you had forgotten about me.

1119
43:42.260 --> 43:43.680
They call each other by their nicknames.

1120
43:43.920 --> 43:45.050
Are they really just friends?

1121
43:47.760 --> 43:48.880
When you talked to Danis,

1122
43:48.900 --> 43:50.640
she said that the box she was carrying

1123
43:50.660 --> 43:51.920
belonged to the director of the orphanage.

1124
43:52.080 --> 43:53.200
Where?

1125
43:53.220 --> 43:54.400
Where is Grandma Gaysorn's photo?

1126
43:55.240 --> 43:57.520
Is this the photo? I can't even see her face.

1127
43:57.580 --> 43:58.980
You should call the director

1128
43:59.000 --> 44:00.960
and ask her if this photo is hers.

1129
44:00.980 --> 44:02.560
It's probably too late to call her now.

1130
44:02.580 --> 44:03.240
- Huh? - Huh?

1131
44:05.120 --> 44:05.800
Don't tell me...

1132
44:08.640 --> 44:12.120
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

1133
44:12.200 --> 44:15.880
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

1134
44:18.440 --> 44:23.920
♫Every step we take has a meaning♫

1135
44:25.670 --> 44:30.560
♫No path is ever meaningless♫

1136
44:32.800 --> 44:38.940
♫As long as our hearts keep searching♫

1137
44:39.880 --> 44:44.440
♫One day, we'll find what we're yearning for♫

1138
44:44.460 --> 44:48.000
♫Walking alone is fine, but it's better when you're by my side♫

1139
44:48.020 --> 44:51.620
♫It won't be lonely when you're here to walk beside♫

1140
44:51.640 --> 44:55.160
♫Like a love that waits, waits at the D Dorm♫

1141
44:55.180 --> 44:57.460
♫Like a love that remains, remains at the dorm♫

1142
44:57.480 --> 45:04.360
♫Meaningful love and good things await on every path♫

1143
45:04.540 --> 45:11.280
♫It might not be a coincidence that we get to meet♫

1144
45:11.750 --> 45:18.900
♫There might be hidden meanings on the path beneath our feet♫

1145
45:18.920 --> 45:25.970
♫Perhaps the D Dorm is what led me to meet you♫

1146
45:25.990 --> 45:29.590
[The D Dorm]
